{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791140593,"nonce":"NA3cngivrIcL63WaXh0uSMTiyNY=","message":"Fixed upstream: in taffy 0.14.0 (latest), determine_container_main_size scales a shrinking item's fraction by f32_max(1.0, item.flex_shrink) * item.inner_flex_basis, the same factor its contribution multiplies back by, so a flex-shrink: 0 item with margin-left: -10 counts 30 as it should. 0.6.3 divides by f32_max(1.0, flex_shrink * inner_flex_basis) and multiplies by max(1, flex_shrink) * inner_flex_basis. Taffy is Blinc's dependency (workspace taffy 0.6); handed to the Blinc session to upgrade or patch that line. The avatar group workaround (flex-shrink: 1) stays until then.","files":null}]}